{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: contract amendment 3, checks and evidence reuse. Close the gaps lanes A, G and the jj follow-ups found in the check, carry and snapshot path, so the integrated Room and the checker service agree on one written contract. MCP-specific changes stay with the separate MCP amendment.","body":{"conditions":"(1) A sealed check-carried system event (or equivalent) so carry-rule decisions on checks are recorded and replayable; until then the contract states that check carry fails closed. (2) Runner environment attestation: where the runner digest comes from (pinned in CheckerConfig and/or attested by the checker service), so R-CARRY-6 compares the current environment with the earlier check's rather than reusing the earlier value. (3) Scoped (filtered) checks: a fixed, reproducible snapshot commit format (tree, parents, identity, time), the rule that a filtered CheckJob.integration is that snapshot commit, how it binds to the canonical integration, and which party issues jobs. (4) Check jobs: job authentication (signed jobs or the trusted service-binding boundary stated as a rule), the gitAuthEnv format, an advisory flag for checks/obligations, base commit and volatile flag on jobs, and that a signed check's volatile flag must equal its configuration. (5) Decide and record: a bounded Room-owned fact about the proposed head's root entries for policy (needed for a whole-head jj conflict check) - add it or keep it explicitly open with a reason; and the Room read lane F's jj history view needs (a generation's commits base..head with headers and bounded trees or interdiffs) - add it or keep it open. (6) Changes are additive where possible; the report lists required edits for lanes A, G, E, F, L and D; npm run typecheck and every package test pass at the amended head.","target_head":"0ad679370d50027121f51ea00c4dbc82cb670373","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef94